    faqs: [{"question":"What conversion rate can an AI sales agent reach on a small catalog?","answer":"North Sole converted 32.52% of chats into orders across 46 days, roughly one in three. Small catalogs with a single branching decision are close to the ideal shape for a website sales agent, because the agent has one job and can do it well."},{"question":"How much of North Sole's revenue involves the AI agent?","answer":"50.32% of store revenue in the 46-day window was AI-influenced, meaning the shopper engaged the Website Agent before purchasing. That share is high because the catalog is small and the purchase decision is explanation-heavy."},{"question":"How does an AI agent sell a product that deliberately has no arch support?","answer":"By carrying the argument rather than avoiding it. The agent is trained on North Sole's position that arch support and heel lift defeat the purpose of a barefoot shoe. Product Info was 49.6% of all classified intent, shoppers arrive needing exactly that explanation."},{"question":"What channels did North Sole connect first, and why?","answer":"Only the Website Agent. North Sole's demand is search- and referral-led rather than social, and the buying decision happens on the product page. Spreading a small traffic base across channels where the brand has no audience would have diluted it."},{"question":"What was North Sole using before YourLio AI?","answer":"No conversational layer at all. Pre-sale questions were answered by a static FAQ page and a size chart published as an image. Both are now available inside the chat at the moment the question is asked."}],
    playbook: [{"lead":"A small catalog is an advantage, not a limitation","text":"Three SKUs with one branching decision produced the fourth highest conversion rate of the fifteen brands here."},{"lead":"Put your size chart in HTML, not a PNG","text":"Sizing is one of the highest-intent query clusters in footwear, and an image forfeits all of it."},{"lead":"Answer inside the customer's mental model","text":"Shoppers arrive using the category's vocabulary, not yours. Correcting them costs the sale; answering them and then explaining does not."},{"lead":"Name products the way people search","text":"Invented product names carry no search demand. Adding the category term loses nothing and gains the query."},{"lead":"Nudge before they leave","text":"On a small catalog the failure is not a wrong answer, it is a shopper who never asked."}],
    cta: {"headline":"One in three chats becomes an order.","body":"See what a 30-day YourLio pilot looks like on your catalog."},
    provenance: "Published 2026-09-08 · Last updated 2026-09-08 · Window 24 July 2026 to 7 September 2026 (46 days), measured from YourLio daily snapshots. Revenue amounts, order counts and average order values are not published.",
    content: {"introduction":"North Sole makes flat, zero-drop cushioning insoles for barefoot and minimalist shoes, no arch support, no heel lift, dual-layer foam, made in the USA. Founded by John Bergervoet after years standing on concrete floors, the brand has narrowed to three products: Legacy at 6mm, LegacyThree at 3mm, and the bundle of both, carrying 845 reviews between them. Sold direct from northsole.co out of Minnetonka, Minnesota, North Sole runs its entire pre-sale chat on the YourLio Website Agent.","sections":[{"title":"Challenge: three products, and the whole sale rides on two questions","paragraphs":["North Sole sells against its own category. Every mainstream competitor sells arch support and heel lift; North Sole's product deliberately has neither, and its bundle page says so outright, most insoles \"'fix' this by adding arch support and heel lift, which forces your foot out of its natural position and defeats the whole point of going barefoot.\"","That makes the purchase explanation-dependent in a way a product grid cannot solve. The chat data shows it precisely: the two dominant themes across the window were **size certainty and fit inside shoes**, and **choosing between Legacy, LegacyThree and the bundle**. Nearly every chat is one of two questions.","There is a third pattern the brand did not expect. Shoppers arrive asking about plantar fasciitis and foot pain (the exact framing North Sole positions away from) and about wide toe-box and zero-drop compatibility with specific shoes they already own. The agent has to answer honestly inside someone else's mental model without either overclaiming a medical benefit or losing the sale.","The site made this harder than necessary. The sizing chart is published as a single image, so its content is unreadable to search engines, to answer engines and to screen readers, and unavailable to a shopper right at the moment they need it."]},{"title":"Solution: one agent trained on the thickness decision","paragraphs":["The **Website Agent** went live on 24 July 2026 as North Sole's only channel. No WhatsApp, no Instagram, no email flows. One surface, one job.","**AI Sales Chat** was trained on the full catalog, the sizing data that had been locked inside a PNG, the trim-to-fit instructions, the transition-period guidance from the FAQ, and (critically) the brand's argument against arch support. It reads which page the shopper is on: someone on the LegacyThree page asking about standing on concrete all day gets pointed to the 6mm Legacy, not a list of both.","**Smart Nudges** cover the shoppers who would have left without asking. On a catalog this small, the failure mode is not a wrong answer; it is a shopper who never asks which thickness they need and closes the tab."]},{"title":"Strategy: how North Sole runs it now","paragraphs":["Conversion is the whole story here. North Sole did not add traffic; it converted more of what it already had.","**Let the agent make the thickness call.** Product Info was the single largest intent at 281 chats, followed by Product Browsing at 147 and Product Discovery at 69, 88% of all classified intent was pre-sale, not support. The Legacy + LegacyThree bundle was the most-discussed product on all 46 days of the window, ahead of either single item. The agent is not deflecting tickets here; it is doing the selling.","**Answer inside the shopper's mental model.** Shoppers ask about plantar fasciitis and about whether the insole will fit a specific pair of Merrell zero-drop shoes. The agent answers the question that was actually asked, explains what the product does and does not do, and lets the shopper decide. That is the difference between a 32.52% conversion rate and an argument.","**Free the sizing data from the image.** The most repeated shopper question in the window was a version of \"Will this fit my shoes?\" The agent now answers it, but the underlying chart still lives only as a picture on the product page. Publishing the same table as real HTML would earn organic and answer-engine traffic for a query cluster the brand currently forfeits entirely."]}]},
