    faqs: [{"question":"What is the highest chat to order rate YourLio has measured?","answer":"36.7%, at Ugees, across over 1,500 chats between 1 July and 7 September 2026. It is the highest rate among twenty brands measured, and it comes from a single-product catalog where almost every chat is the same pack decision."},{"question":"How does Instagram comment-to-DM work for a small brand?","answer":"Instagram AI auto-replies to comments on posts and reels with the right product and sends a direct buy link into the DM. Instagram carried 461 of Ugees' over 1,500 chats (24.1%) which for a category-creating brand is a meaningful share of discovery."},{"question":"Why does a single-product brand convert so well through chat?","answer":"Because the decision is narrow. With one product line and several pack formats, nearly every chat is \"which pack\" rather than \"which product\", and the agent can explain the refill economics in one exchange."},{"question":"How should an AI agent handle discount questions?","answer":"Specifically. 332 of Ugees' chats were about offers (17.4% of volume) and the recorded objection was shoppers asking repeatedly and still not adding to cart. An agent that knows the exact live promotion resolves that; one that says \"yes, we have offers\" does not."},{"question":"What channels does Ugees run YourLio AI on?","answer":"Three: the Website Agent for the pack decision, Instagram AI for comment-to-DM discovery, and WhatsApp AI for order status and reorder on a consumable product."}],
    playbook: [{"lead":"A narrow catalog is a conversion advantage","text":"One product line and several formats produced the best conversion rate across twenty brands."},{"lead":"Comment to DM is discovery infrastructure for category-creating brands","text":"A comment is someone who just learned the product exists."},{"lead":"Answer the offer question with a number, not a yes","text":"Shoppers asked repeatedly and still did not convert; that is a stalled decision, not a browsing pattern."},{"lead":"Explain the refill economics","text":"\"Why buy refill instead of two bottles?\" was the single most asked question in the account, and it is a basket-size question."},{"lead":"Put reorder on WhatsApp","text":"A consumable's second purchase should not need a website visit."}],
    cta: {"headline":"A one-product catalog converted better than catalogs a thousand times its size.","body":"See what a 30-day YourLio pilot looks like on your catalog."},
    provenance: "Published 2026-09-08 · Last updated 2026-09-08 · Window 1 July 2026 to 7 September 2026 (69 days), measured from YourLio daily snapshots. Revenue amounts, order counts and average order values are not published.",
    content: {"introduction":"Ugees makes a specialist liquid detergent for undergarments and delicates, sold as a bottle, a travel pack, a refill and several combos. Founded by Rahul Tyagi and Samiksha Yadav, the brand appeared on Shark Tank India and took investment from Anupam Mittal; it is plant-based, IFRA-certified on fragrance and uses 100% biodegradable surfactants. Sold direct from ugees.in and through BigBasket, Flipkart, FirstCry and Smytten, Ugees runs three conversational channels on YourLio AI.","sections":[{"title":"Challenge: one product, and a pack decision nobody understands","paragraphs":["Ugees essentially sells one thing. The complexity is not the product, it is the format: a bottle, a travel pack of two, a refill pack, and three different combos. The single most asked question in the whole account was **\"Why buy Refill instead of 2 regular bottles?\":** a pure merchandising question that decides basket size.","The second problem is category education. Because the product is a niche most people have never bought, shoppers ask whether it can be used by both men and women, whether it is safe, and how it differs from ordinary detergent. The recorded theme is **unisex suitability for intimate wash:** that is a first-purchase objection on a product the customer did not know existed.","The third is offers. The recorded objection is precise and expensive: shoppers asked \"Any offers?\" repeatedly **and still did not add to cart**. An offer the customer cannot resolve is worse than no offer, because it stalls a decision that was otherwise made.","And demand arrives socially. Instagram carried a meaningful share of chats, comments on posts and reels, from an audience discovering a category rather than comparing brands."]},{"title":"Solution: three channels, one decision","paragraphs":["The **Website Agent** owns the pack decision. Refill versus bottle versus combo is the entire conversion event, and the agent explains the economics rather than showing six similar cards.","**Instagram AI** handles comment to DM. A comment on a post gets an automatic reply with the right product and a direct buy link straight into the DM, which matters for a brand whose discovery is social and whose audience is finding out the category exists.","**WhatsApp AI** carries order status and reorder. This is a consumable, so the second purchase should not require a website visit at all.","The **Nudge Engine** addresses the offer stall directly. Because the agent knows the live promotion and the free-shipping threshold, \"Any offers?\" gets an answer specific enough to act on rather than a yes."]},{"title":"Strategy: how Ugees runs it now","paragraphs":["36.7% of chats end in an order. That is the highest rate across all twenty brands in the YourLio dataset, and it comes from a very particular shape.","**A one-product catalog converts if the pack logic is explained.** Product Info led at over 1,000 chats and Product Discovery at 470. With one product line and several formats, almost every chat is the same decision, which is why the conversion rate is so high. The refill pack and the combos were among the most-discussed items throughout the window.","**Treat Instagram comments as inventory.** Instagram carried 461 chats, nearly a quarter. For a category-creating brand, a comment is a person who just found out the product exists. Comment to DM turns that moment into a buy link instead of a like.","**Make the offer answerable.** 332 chats were classified as Offer/Rewards, 17.4% of all volume. The recorded objection is that shoppers asked about offers repeatedly and still did not add to cart. An agent that knows the exact live promotion converts that question instead of parking it."]}]},
