    content: {"introduction":"Nysh makes self-heating body, hand and foot warmers under the WARMEE brand and pain-relief patches under BluHeat, using an air-activated exothermic reaction rather than electricity. Established in 2001 by a team of chemical engineers and operated by Pantheon PharmChem in Mumbai, the company runs its own manufacturing and R&D at Tarapur, unusual in a category where most brands outsource. Sold from nysh.in and through pharmacy channels, Nysh runs three conversational surfaces on YourLio AI.","sections":[{"title":"Challenge: shoppers don't know the category, let alone the product","paragraphs":["Nysh is the only brand documented here where **Product Discovery outranks Product Info**. That inversion is the whole story: most shoppers arriving on the site have never bought an air-activated warmer and do not know what it is, how long it lasts, or whether it is safe to use every day.","The recorded themes are exactly that shape: **product matching by target area:** back, neck and shoulders, cramps; **heat duration expectations** across pack sizes; **daily-use safety confidence gaps**; and WARMEE needing to be explained as a cold-weather, air-activated warmer in the first place.","The most common opening in the account was a generic one (\"Help me find something in WARMEE\") which is what a shopper types when the catalog vocabulary means nothing to them yet. The second was \"How long does the heat last?\"","And the recorded objections are unusually consistent: three of the four are about **safety guidance the agent could not confirm**. Whether a product is safe for daily use, how frequently it can be applied, and how many hours of heat to expect per format. Those are knowledge-base gaps, not model failures, and they are the highest-value thing to fix in this account."]},{"title":"Solution: explain the category, then match the need","paragraphs":["The **Website Agent** carries the explanation. Before a shopper can pick between a pack of five and a pack of ten, they need to understand what the product does and how long it lasts, so the agent teaches the category and then narrows.","**AI Quiz and Discovery** handles the shoppers who open with \"help me find something\". A catalog organised by body area and pack size is not browsable by someone who does not yet know which body area applies to their problem.","**Instagram AI** and **WhatsApp AI** are both live. Both are early in their rollout in this window and the Website Agent carries the large majority of chats.","The honest finding: the agent's ceiling here is the knowledge base, not the model. Daily-use safety and heat-duration guidance are the two things shoppers asked for most and the two things the agent could least often confirm. Publishing that guidance is the single highest -leverage change available to this account."]},{"title":"Strategy: how Nysh runs it now","paragraphs":["A niche account, early in its channel rollout, with an unusually clean signal about what to fix.","**Teach the category before selling the pack.** 376 chats were Product Discovery, the only account here where discovery leads. A shopper who does not know what an air-activated warmer is cannot evaluate a pack of five against a pack of ten.","**Publish the safety and duration guidance.** Three of the four recorded objections are about daily-use safety and heat duration the agent could not confirm. That is a content gap with a clear owner and a clear fix, and it sits directly on the path to purchase.","**Let the quiz carry a catalog nobody can browse.** Body area plus pack size is not a structure a first-time buyer can navigate. Guided discovery converts a described problem (back pain, period cramps, cold hands) into a format recommendation."]}]},
